<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tirich Mir</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tirich Mir is the highest mountain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-kush">Hindu Kush</a>, rising to 7,708 metres in Chitral district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-frontier-province">Khyber Pakhtunkhwa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. It dominates the Chitral valley and appears in local legend as the home of fairies. It was first climbed in 1950 by a Norwegian expedition led by Arne Næss.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tirich-mir.jpg" alt="Tirich Mir" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: KaleemUllah550 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tirich_Mir_(The_Kingdom_Of_Djinns_And_Fairies).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
